WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.510
The group baseline has the lowest
overall validation mean absolute error,

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.310
ninety one point five seven.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.570
It also beats the representative forest
on the defined working day rush slice.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.770
But June reverses that comparison:

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.710
groups has error near one
hundred and forty three,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.830
while the forest is near
ninety point eight eight.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.010
The deep tree is also much better in June.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.690
We keep that tradeoff visible rather than
describing one function as uniformly best.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.410
The forest value here belongs to one
retained seed seventeen artifact,

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.790
distinct from its earlier three
seed configuration average.

00:00:40.003 --> 00:00:45.723
The previous study selected configurations
using overall validation mean absolute

00:00:45.723 --> 00:00:49.333
error, giving each
observed hour equal weight.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.873
We have not agreed a June only objective,

00:00:53.443 --> 00:00:54.953
a special rush penalty

00:00:55.563 --> 00:00:57.473
or a monetary cost function.

00:00:57.843 --> 00:00:59.453
Those would be different questions.

00:01:00.443 --> 00:01:05.323
Selecting a forest just because one
inspected slice is favorable would

00:01:05.323 --> 00:01:08.693
silently change the objective
after seeing its result.

00:01:09.423 --> 00:01:15.073
Constructing a routed ensemble would also
be another fitted or selected function,

00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:17.153
beyond this diagnostic review.

00:01:18.183 --> 00:01:21.303
We retain the prior groups
and raw output choice,

00:01:21.303 --> 00:01:26.013
and record the later period weakness
as part of the candidate handoff.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.860
The handoff copies the exact original
selected group model into a candidate

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.870
model file.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.790
Its bytes are identical to the
previously fitted artifact,

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.250
and the candidate configuration
records their hash.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.290
No fitting call is made
during this review.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.930
The configuration also retains
data and split identities,

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.110
model feature order,
fitting source, review protocol

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.010
and used calendar fields.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:01.340
The old fit source and the current
analysis source remain separate provenance

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:06.030
records, rather than rewriting history
as though the review trained the model.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:11.570
This makes the exact function being handed
forward inspectable and reproducible.

00:02:13.728 --> 00:02:18.738
The candidate output is a raw floating
point estimate in rentals per hour.

00:02:19.128 --> 00:02:24.078
Group means are already nonnegative,
so no clipping or rounding is added.

00:02:25.228 --> 00:02:29.378
A valid absent key uses the
training only global fallback.

00:02:29.808 --> 00:02:32.498
Invalid inputs are
rejected before prediction.

00:02:33.628 --> 00:02:36.438
The same configuration
carries the known schema,

00:02:37.248 --> 00:02:39.698
ordered features,
historical date boundaries

00:02:40.128 --> 00:02:41.498
and issue lead convention.

00:02:42.588 --> 00:02:44.398
If one of these policies changed,

00:02:45.088 --> 00:02:49.028
equal parameter bytes would no longer
establish identical behavior for all

00:02:49.028 --> 00:02:49.618
requests.

00:02:50.648 --> 00:02:53.878
We therefore freeze the contract
beside the fitted values,

00:02:54.068 --> 00:02:57.398
rather than leaving future application
code to guess their meaning.

00:02:59.707 --> 00:03:01.737
Ninety six source checks pass.

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:05.757
The independent audit recomputes
fourteen prediction files,

00:03:06.027 --> 00:03:09.297
six hundred and eighty six
slice summaries, time groups,

00:03:09.607 --> 00:03:10.837
gap sensitive correlation,

00:03:11.407 --> 00:03:14.297
largest misses and the
calendar level comparison.

00:03:15.147 --> 00:03:18.517
It also verifies candidate
bytes and source, dependency

00:03:18.887 --> 00:03:20.237
and artifact identities.

00:03:20.927 --> 00:03:25.987
An isolated installed wheel check confirms
package behavior while excluding private

00:03:25.987 --> 00:03:27.157
notes and runs.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:31.507
These checks establish implemented
behavior and the retained numerical

00:03:31.507 --> 00:03:32.437
result.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.927
They do not establish that the
learner has explained the reasoning,

00:03:35.927 --> 00:03:38.837
or that an operational decision improves.

00:03:39.407 --> 00:03:42.267
The written records were completed
before these section companions,

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.877
and remain the full source for review.

00:03:47.082 --> 00:03:49.112
The candidate retains its weaknesses:

00:03:49.902 --> 00:03:52.752
the same hour and day type ignores month,

00:03:53.142 --> 00:03:56.252
and working day rush
deficits remain substantial.

00:03:56.982 --> 00:04:01.052
Observed rentals do not measure
unmet demand or inventory,

00:04:01.442 --> 00:04:05.212
and this review adds no
calibrated predictive interval.

00:04:05.982 --> 00:04:10.012
Serving and fresh process
recovery are explicitly pending,

00:04:10.442 --> 00:04:13.352
while reserved test
outcomes remain unopened.

00:04:13.942 --> 00:04:17.272
Repeated validation inspection
is development evidence

00:04:17.662 --> 00:04:19.952
and can make selected scores optimistic.

00:04:20.922 --> 00:04:21.912
Before advancing,

00:04:22.082 --> 00:04:26.852
explain why the valid June request
gets the same group mean as January,

00:04:27.142 --> 00:04:30.452
and why that can coexist
with the best overall score.

00:04:30.922 --> 00:04:34.612
Those questions connect the
fitted function, chosen objective

00:04:35.062 --> 00:04:37.332
and honest limits of the current evidence.

